# Make theia build work in pnpm strict mode.
# theia 1.73.1's generated esbuild.mjs runs under the browser app
# directory and imports esbuild + its plugins (which are pulled in
# transitively via @theia/application-manager). pnpm strict mode
# does not hoist these, so we hoist everything.
#
# DK-P3-7: keep shamefully-hoist=true. Switching to public-hoist-pattern
# alone is not enough — Theia’s generated esbuild + plugin graph and
# Electron native rebuilds still resolve packages from the app cwd, and
# a partial hoist has broken @theia/*/node resolution in this monorepo.
# Known consumers that need cwd-visible resolution: esbuild (+ plugins),
# @theia/application-manager, electron/native rebuild helpers.
# Follow-up: ADR to trial public-hoist-pattern=[esbuild*,@esbuild*,@theia/*]
# once a clean install+browser+desktop build proves no phantom-dep breaks.
# Prefer documenting phantom-dep risk over a risky hoist change for now.
shamefully-hoist=true
